Z||000000||lowfierogt||11-14-2001||10:35 PM||||Hey all,, I have a new project car and need some help with picking a color.    im making my 85 GT, become a fastback, 4 speed with 4.10, 350 V8 or 327.     Im starting with ripping every panel off the car, then taking all the interior out.  Sandblasting everything, tranny conversion...there's an auto in there now.  Mounting engine and painting.  What do you think?  It's black now, but not sure if I want to keep it black.   I will be taking pictures of progress.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://lowfierogt.no-ip.com/sig1.jpg">    <BR>http://lowfierogt.no-ip.com<BR>86 1/2 GT<BR>85 GT<BR>87 coupe daily driver over 300k miles||||reg||5
Z||000001||California Kid||11-14-2001||10:47 PM||||Don't sandblast the sheet metal as it will strip the galvanized electroplate. Use a media blast that only removes paint. Also you need a special metal prep for galvanized steel so that the new paint will stick to it, you can get it at any automotive painters supply store.  Naturally you can sand blast any areas that have red corrosion as the galvanized is depleated already.<P>Have fun on your project.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Signature_7.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||lowfierogt||11-14-2001||11:01 PM||||thanks..<P>I never knew that.<P>I just mainly want to get rid for the suface rust.   Fiero's are known to rust up here.  <P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://lowfierogt.no-ip.com/sig1.jpg">    <BR>http://lowfierogt.no-ip.com<BR>86 1/2 GT<BR>85 GT<BR>87 coupe daily driver over 300k miles||||reg||1
Z||000003||jelly2m8||11-14-2001||11:02 PM||||I'd advise against the 4.10 4spd in a V8.<P>I did that first time around, and 1st gear was absolutely useless ( 'cept for frying the tires...).<P>Even on steep hills, I took off in 2nd gear.<BR>The car was effectively a 3 spd.<P>Also even with the V8 you will only have a top speed of 130mph at most.<P>I spun a rod bearing in my first motor trying to go faster....||||reg||1
Z||000004||lowfierogt||11-14-2001||11:20 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by jelly2m8:<BR><B>I'd advise against the 4.10 4spd in a V8.<P>I did that first time around, and 1st gear was absolutely useless ( 'cept for frying the tires...).<P>Even on steep hills, I took off in 2nd gear.<BR>The car was effectively a 3 spd.<P>Also even with the V8 you will only have a top speed of 130mph at most.<P>I spun a rod bearing in my first motor trying to go faster....</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Its going to be a 1/4 mile ride only.   I was thinking 5 speed, but don't have the tranny.    Hope to get a 7000 rpm engine.   I want to get into the 11s.<BR>||||reg||1
